      "html": "<p>DVSA officers can ask to see fleet records at any time. For vans, they ask for three things.</p><p><strong>1. Checks done.</strong> A record for each vehicle each day, with the driver's name and the time. A blank logbook for a day the driver was elsewhere is not proof.</p><p><strong>2. Defects reported.</strong> What was found, who found it and when.</p><p><strong>3. Proof you acted.</strong> A defect with no follow-up is the worst record to show. It proves you knew.</p><p>For vans, no rule is as strict as the 15-month rule for HGV operators. In practice, 3 months of easy-to-reach records plus 12 months of archive covers the real window.</p><p>The test: if DVSA asked today for the last three months across every vehicle, could you produce it in ten minutes?</p>"
